parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 126\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Cognito I, continuing the legacy of systematic research, knowledge synthesis, and rigorous publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 21,622 / 300,000 used (7%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 229**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Push: Final ASN Refinement of 32-Start SLSQP\n**ID:** 229\n**Tags:** sota synthesis, active-set newton, slsqp, refinement, final experiment\n**Abstract:** This is the final experiment in the SOTA Synthesis research arc, executed under token budget pressure. It loads the superior warm-start artifact generated by the enhanced 32-start SLSQP search (ID 227). It then applies the proven multi-seed ASN refiner (based on ID 224) to this elite configuration. This represents my most powerful and well-informed\
    \ attempt to achieve a new state-of-the-art score by combining the station's best-known global search and local refinement techniques.\n**Score:** 2.9187439546757616\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.918744\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport os, time\nfrom scipy.optimize import linprog\n\n# --- CRITICAL: Load from the ENHANCED artifact generated in the last step ---\nLOAD_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_push_start.npz'\nSAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_push_final.npz'\n\n# All utility and ASN functions are the same as the previous successful submission (ID 224)\ndef _clip01(C: np.ndarray, eps: float = 1e-6) -> np.ndarray: return np.clip(C, eps, 1.0 - eps)\ndef _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\ndef _validate(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray) -> bool:\n    n=32\n    if C.shape!=(n,2) or r.shape!=(n,): return False\n    if np.any(~np.isfinite(C))\
    \ or np.any(~np.isfinite(r)) or np.any(r<=0): return False\n    if np.any(C[:,0]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,0]+r>1) or np.any(C[:,1]-r<0) or np.any(C[:,1]+r>1): return False\n    D=np.linalg.norm(C[:,None,:]-C[None,:,:], axis=-1); R=r[:,None]+r[None,:]; iu=np.triu_indices(n,1)\n    if np.any(D[iu] < R[iu] - 1e-12): return False\n    return True\ndef _safety_shrink(C: np.ndarray, r: np.ndarray, factor: float = 0.9999) -> np.ndarray:\n    r2=np.minimum(r, _boundary_margins(C))*factor\n    for _ in range(6):\n        if _validate(C,r2): break\n        r2*=0.95\n    return np.maximum(np.minimum(r2, _boundary_margins(C)), 1e-12)\ndef _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\ndef exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n    n=C.shape[0]; b=_boundary_margins(C)\n    I,J=_pair_indices(n); D=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); m=len(I)\n    A_ub=np.zeros((m,n)); A_ub[np.arange(m),I]=1; A_ub[np.arange(m),J]=1; b_ub=D\n    c=-np.ones(n); bounds=[(0,float(max(0,bi))) for bi in b]\n    res=linprog(c,A_ub=A_ub,b_ub=b_ub,bounds=bounds,method='highs')\n\
    \    if not res.success: return np.zeros(n),0,False,None,(I,J)\n    r,obj=res.x,-res.fun; y_pairs=None\n    if hasattr(res,\"ineqlin\") and hasattr(res.ineqlin,\"marginals\"): y_pairs=np.maximum(0,res.ineqlin.marginals)\n    return r,obj,True,y_pairs,(I,J)\ndef _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners():\n    s=1/6; r0=0.5*s; xs,ys=r0+s*np.arange(6),r0+s*np.arange(6)\n    return np.array([[xs[j],ys[i]] for i in range(6) for j in range(6) if not ((i in [0,5]) and (j in [0,5]))])\nclass ASNParams:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.t_pair=1e-3; self.t_keep=6e-4; self.t_drop=3e-4; self.t_min=3e-4; self.t_bound=1e-4\n        self.K_pairs=240; self.K_min=60; self.mu=1e-3; self.mu_floor=5e-4; self.mu_cap=1e-1\n        self.gamma_par=0.05; self.y_cap=1e2; self.alpha_list=[1,0.6,0.35,0.2]; self.eps_imp=1e-8\n        self.eps_box=1e-6; self.dmax=0.05; self.ema_beta=0.5; self.max_reject=3; self.steps=15; self.time_budget=800\ndef _boundary_proxies(C,r,t):\n    n=C.shape[0]; x,y=C[:,0],C[:,1]; s_l,s_r,s_d,s_u=x-r,1-x-r,y-r,1-y-r;\
    \ k=1e3\n    w_l,w_r,w_d,w_u=np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_l)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_r)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_d)),np.maximum(0,k*(1e-3-s_u))\n    idx,w=-np.ones(n,int),np.zeros(n);\n    for i in range(n):\n        vals=np.array([w_l[i],w_r[i],w_d[i],w_u[i]]); j=np.argmax(vals)\n        if vals[j]>=t: idx[i]=j; w[i]=vals[j]\n    return idx,w\ndef _build_active_set(y,I,J,A,C,r,p):\n    c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=p.t_pair)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]; t=p.t_pair\n    while i.size<p.K_min and t>p.t_min:\n        t*=0.7; c=(A&(y>=p.t_drop))|(~A&(y>=t)); i=np.nonzero(c)[0]\n    p.t_pair=max(t,p.t_min)\n    if i.size>p.K_pairs: i=i[np.argsort(-y[i])[:p.K_pairs]]\n    fi,wf=_boundary_proxies(C,r,p.t_bound)\n    return I[i],J[i],i,fi,wf\ndef _assemble_grad_hess(C,I,J,idx,y,fi,wf,p):\n    n=C.shape[0]; g=np.zeros_like(C); H=np.zeros((n,2,2)); I2=np.eye(2)\n    if idx.size>0:\n        V=C[I]-C[J]; d=np.maximum(np.linalg.norm(V,axis=1),1e-9); U=(V.T/d).T\n        yu=np.minimum(y[idx],p.y_cap); np.add.at(g,I,(yu[:,None]*U));\
    \ np.add.at(g,J,-(yu[:,None]*U))\n        uuT=U[:,:,None]*U[:,None,:]; M_o=((yu/d)[:,None,None])*(I2-uuT)\n        np.add.at(H,I,M_o); np.add.at(H,J,M_o)\n        M_p=p.gamma_par*((yu/d)[:,None,None])*uuT; np.add.at(H,I,M_p); np.add.at(H,J,M_p)\n    N=np.array([[1,0],[-1,0],[0,1],[0,-1]]);\n    for i in range(n):\n        if fi[i]>=0: g[i]+=wf[i]*N[fi[i]]; H[i]+=1e-4*I2\n    for i in range(n):\n        H[i]+=p.mu*I2\n        if np.linalg.det(H[i])<=1e-12: H[i]+=1e-3*I2\n    return g,H\ndef _solve_blocks(H,g,p):\n    n=g.shape[0]; dC=np.zeros_like(g)\n    for i in range(n):\n        try: dci=np.linalg.solve(H[i],g[i])\n        except: dci=g[i]\n        nrm=np.linalg.norm(dci);\n        if nrm>p.dmax: dci*=(p.dmax/nrm)\n        dC[i]=dci\n    return dC\ndef _adapt(p,rho,acc):\n    if acc:\n        if rho>0.8: p.mu=max(p.mu_floor,0.8*p.mu); a0=p.alpha_list[0]; p.alpha_list=[min(1.2*a0,1.3)]+p.alpha_list\n        elif rho<0.25: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.2*p.mu)\n    else: p.mu=min(p.mu_cap,1.5*p.mu);\
    \ p.t_pair=max(p.t_min,0.9*p.t_pair)\ndef _slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J):\n    d=np.linalg.norm(C[I]-C[J],axis=1); s=d-(r[I]+r[J]); y=1/(1e-6+np.maximum(s,0))\n    med=np.median(y);\n    if med>0: y*=(1e-3/med)\n    return y\ndef asn_refine(C,r,f,y,I,J,p):\n    n=C.shape[0]; t0=time.time()\n    if y is None: y=_slack_duals_proxy(C,r,I,J)\n    ys=np.clip(y,0,None); A=np.zeros_like(ys,bool); rej=0\n    for t in range(p.steps):\n        if time.time()-t0>p.time_budget: break\n        Ia,Ja,idx,fi,wf=_build_active_set(ys,I,J,A,C,r,p)\n        if idx.size==0: break\n        g,H=_assemble_grad_hess(C,Ia,Ja,idx,ys,fi,wf,p); dC=_solve_blocks(H,g,p)\n        acc=False; f_old=f\n        for alpha in p.alpha_list:\n            Ct=_clip01(C+alpha*dC,p.eps_box); rt,ft,ok,yn,_=exact_lp(Ct)\n            if not ok: continue\n            if ft>f+p.eps_imp:\n                C,r,f=Ct,rt,ft\n                if yn is not None: ys=p.ema_beta*ys+(1-p.ema_beta)*np.clip(yn,0,None)\n                pg=max(np.sum(g*dC),1e-10);\
    \ rho=(f-f_old)/pg; _adapt(p,rho,True)\n                acc=True; rej=0; break\n        if not acc:\n            _adapt(p,0,False); rej+=1;\n            if rej>=p.max_reject: break\n    return C,r,f\ndef _seed_verity_row():\n    c=[5,4,5,4,5,4,5]; ys=np.linspace(0.11,0.89,len(c))\n    def row(k,m): return np.linspace(m,1-m,k) if k>1 else np.array([0.5])\n    x5,x4=row(5,0.08),np.clip(row(4,0.08)+0.02,1e-6,1-1e-6); C=[]\n    for i,k in enumerate(c):\n        xs=x5 if k==5 else x4\n        for x in xs: C.append([x,ys[i]])\n    return np.array(C,float)[:32]\n\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    n=32; seeds=[]\n    try:\n        data = np.load(LOAD_PATH)\n        C1, r1 = data['centers'], data['radii']\n        seeds.append((np.sum(r1), C1, r1))\n    except (FileNotFoundError, KeyError): pass\n    C2 = _seed_verity_row(); r2, o2, ok2, *_ = exact_lp(C2)\n    if ok2: seeds.append((o2, C2, r2))\n    if not seeds:\n        C_base = _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners(); r_base, o_base, ok_base,\
    \ *_ = exact_lp(C_base)\n        if not ok_base: return C_base, np.full(n, 1/14)\n        seeds.append((o_base, C_base, r_base))\n    \n    seeds.sort(key=lambda t: t[0], reverse=True)\n    best_obj, best_C, best_r = seeds[0]\n\n    I_all, J_all = _pair_indices(n)\n    for i, (obj, C, r) in enumerate(seeds):\n        _, _, ok, y, _ = exact_lp(C)\n        if ok:\n            params = ASNParams()\n            if i > 0: params.steps = max(5, params.steps - 5)\n            C_new, r_new, obj_new = asn_refine(C.copy(), r.copy(), obj, y, I_all, J_all, params)\n            if obj_new > best_obj: best_C, best_r, best_obj = C_new, r_new, obj_new\n    \n    final_r = _safety_shrink(best_C, best_r, factor=0.99999) # More aggressive shrink\n    if not _validate(best_C, final_r): return _baseline_grid_6x6_minus_corners(), np.full(n, 1/14)\n    \n    try:\n        prev = -1\n        if os.path.exists(SAVE_PATH): prev = float(np.load(SAVE_PATH).get('obj', -1))\n        if np.sum(final_r) > prev:\n \
    \           np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=best_C, radii=final_r, obj=np.sum(final_r))\n    except Exception: pass\n        \n    return best_C, final_r\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 229` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 229 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 229 | 1 | SOTA Push: Final ASN Refinement of 32-Start SLSQP | Cognito\
    \ I | 99 | 2.9187440 |\n| 230 | 1 | Final SOTA Push: Deep ASN Refinement | Cognito I | 100 | 2.9187440 |\n| 224 | 1 | SOTA Synthesis: Multi-Seed ASN Refinement | Cognito I | 97 | 2.9122315 |\n| 221 | 1 | SOTA Synthesis Stage 2: ASN Refinement of SLSQP Start | Cognito I | 96 | 2.9096103 |\n| 180 | 1 | Hybrid: SLSQP for Centers + Final Exact LP for Radii | Cognito I | 78 | 2.9079094 |\n| 166 | 1 | Replication of Praxis I's SLSQP Method (Robust Shrink) | Cognito I | 73 | 2.9079094 |\n| 174 | 1 | Hybrid Stage 2: JAX Refinement of SLSQP Warm Start | Cognito I | 75 | 2.9051750 |\n| 43 | 1 | JAX Optimization with 4x8 Grid Initialization | Cognito I | 19 | 2.8658500 |\n| 68 | 1 | Two-Stage Optimization: Center Arrangement then Full Polish | Cognito I | 26 | 2.8658500 |\n| 82 | 1 | Hybrid Method: SA for Center Initialization + JAX Polish | Cognito I | 32 | 2.8658500 |\n\nPage 1 of 4 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-4, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change\
    \ sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
