tick: 133
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am back at the Research Counter, ready to implement the first step of my new research plan. I will now submit the enhanced generator script. This script increases the `maxiter` option in the `SLSQP` optimizer from 125 to 250. The resulting artifact will be saved to a new file, `sota_improvement_start.npz`, to clearly distinguish it from my previous replication artifacts.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Push Step 1: Deeper Multi-Start SLSQP Generator\"\ntags: \"sota improvement, slsqp, multi-start, warm start, generator\"\nabstract: \"This experiment tests the hypothesis that a deeper search in the generator stage can yield a superior warm-start artifact. This script is a modification of the previous SOTA generator (ID 258), with the max iterations for each of the 32 SLSQP runs doubled from 125 to 250. The best result will be saved to 'storage/cognito/sota_improvement_start.npz' for a subsequent refinement attempt.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from\
    \ scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import os\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n\n      def _seed_praxis_grid(seed):\n          np.random.seed(seed)\n          grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:n]\n          noise = (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.08\n          return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n      def _seed_verity_row():\n          counts = [5, 4, 5, 4, 5, 4, 5]\n          ys = np.linspace(0.11, 0.89, len(counts))\n          def row(k, m): return np.linspace(m, 1 - m, k) if k > 1 else np.array([0.5])\n          x5, x4 = row(5, 0.08), np.clip(row(4, 0.08) + 0.02, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n          C = [[x, ys[i]] for i, k in enumerate(counts) for x in (x5 if k == 5 else x4)]\n          return np.array(C, float)[:32]\n\n      def _seed_verity_farthest(seed):\n          rng = np.random.default_rng(seed)\n          C = [rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, 2)]\n          for _ in range(1, n):\n  \
    \            cand = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, (600, 2))\n              d2 = np.sum((cand[:, np.newaxis, :] - np.array(C)[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, -1)\n              C.append(cand[np.argmax(np.min(np.sqrt(d2), 1))])\n          return np.clip(np.array(C), 0.05, 0.95)\n\n      def objective(x): return -np.sum(x[2::3])\n      def constraints(x):\n          c, r = x.reshape(n, 3)[:, :2], x.reshape(n, 3)[:, 2]\n          cons = [c[:, 0] - r, 1 - c[:, 0] - r, c[:, 1] - r, 1 - c[:, 1] - r]\n          I, J = np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n          dist_sq = np.sum((c[I] - c[J])**2, 1)\n          radii_sum_sq = (r[I] + r[J])**2\n          cons.append(dist_sq - radii_sum_sq)\n          return np.concatenate(cons)\n\n      # --- Enhanced Multi-Start Loop (32 starts) ---\n      num_starts = 32\n      best_score = -1\n      best_packing_params = None\n\n      for i in range(num_starts):\n          if i < 16:\n              initial_centers = _seed_praxis_grid(i)\n          elif i < 24:\n              initial_centers\
    \ = _seed_verity_row()\n          else:\n              initial_centers = _seed_verity_farthest(i)\n          \n          initial_radii = np.full((n,), 0.05)\n          x0 = np.hstack([initial_centers, initial_radii[:, np.newaxis]]).flatten()\n          cons_dict = {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraints}\n          bounds = [(0, 1) if j % 3 < 2 else (1e-12, None) for j in range(n * 3)]\n\n          # --- HYPOTHESIS TEST: Increased search depth ---\n          res = minimize(objective, x0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=cons_dict, options={'maxiter': 250, 'ftol': 1e-10})\n          \n          if -res.fun > best_score:\n              best_score = -res.fun\n              best_packing_params = res.x\n      \n      final_params = best_packing_params.reshape(n, 3)\n      final_centers = final_params[:, :2]\n      final_radii = final_params[:, 2] * (1.0 - 1e-8)\n      \n      SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sota_improvement_start.npz'\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n\
    \      np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=final_centers, radii=final_radii)\n      \n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n```"
