tick: 139
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am ready to submit my new Simulated Annealing generator. The code is a direct implementation of the plan I formulated in the Reflection Chamber. It uses the `exact_lp` function as its energy calculation, employs a hybrid neighborhood function (perturbation and swaps), and follows a slow geometric cooling schedule with robust termination criteria. The resulting artifact will be saved to `sa_generator_artifact.npz`.\n\nThis is Step 1 of my new research arc. The goal is to see if this fundamentally different global search approach can outperform the multi-start SLSQP method.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generator Arc 2, Step 1: Simulated Annealing Generator\"\ntags: \"simulated annealing, generator, global optimization, sota improvement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment introduces a new generator for the SOTA pipeline, replacing multi-start SLSQP with Simulated Annealing (SA). The SA algorithm minimizes an energy function defined by the output of an exact LP solver\
    \ for radii, focusing the search on optimal center configurations. The goal is to produce a superior warm-start artifact. The best configuration found will be saved to 'storage/cognito/sa_generator_artifact.npz'.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import os\n  import time\n\n  # --- Utility functions from previous submissions ---\n  def _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\n  def _seed_praxis_grid(seed):\n      np.random.seed(seed)\n      n=32\n      grid_points = np.stack(np.meshgrid(np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6), np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 6)), -1).reshape(-1, 2)[:n]\n      noise = (np.random.rand(n, 2) - 0.5) * 0.08\n      return np.clip(grid_points + noise, 0.05, 0.95)\n\n  # --- Energy Function for SA ---\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n\
    \      D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n      m = len(I)\n      A_ub = np.zeros((m, n))\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1\n      A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1\n      b_ub = D\n      c = -np.ones(n)\n      bounds = [(0, float(max(0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      # Using 'highs' method as it's proven robust in prior work\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      if not res.success:\n          return np.zeros(n), 0, False # Return 0 score for failure\n      return res.x, -res.fun, True\n\n  # --- Main SA Generator ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      start_time = time.time()\n      TIME_BUDGET = 1180 # seconds\n\n      # Parameters based on reflection\n      T_initial = 0.05\n      T_final = 1e-6\n      alpha = 0.999\n      markov_chain_length = 100\n      max_stagnation = 50 # terminate after 50 temp steps with no improvement\n      \n      # Initialization\n      current_centers = _seed_praxis_grid(seed=42)\n      current_radii,\
    \ current_score, ok = exact_lp(current_centers)\n      if not ok: current_score = 0\n      current_energy = -current_score\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_radii = np.copy(current_radii)\n      best_energy = current_energy\n      \n      T = T_initial\n      stagnation_counter = 0\n\n      # Main SA loop\n      while T > T_final:\n          if time.time() - start_time > TIME_BUDGET:\n              print(\"Time budget exceeded, terminating.\")\n              break\n\n          for _ in range(markov_chain_length):\n              # Neighborhood function\n              candidate_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n              move_type = np.random.rand()\n              \n              if move_type < 0.95: # 95% chance: Single-circle perturbation\n                  i = np.random.randint(n)\n                  max_step = 0.1 # max step size at T_initial\n                  current_step = max_step * (T / T_initial)\n                  perturbation = np.random.normal(0,\
    \ current_step, 2)\n                  candidate_centers[i] += perturbation\n                  candidate_centers[i] = np.clip(candidate_centers[i], 0, 1)\n              else: # 5% chance: Two-circle swap\n                  i, j = np.random.choice(n, 2, replace=False)\n                  candidate_centers[[i, j]] = candidate_centers[[j, i]]\n\n              # Calculate energy of candidate\n              candidate_radii, candidate_score, ok = exact_lp(candidate_centers)\n              if not ok: candidate_score = 0\n              candidate_energy = -candidate_score\n              \n              # Acceptance criterion\n              delta_E = candidate_energy - current_energy\n              if delta_E < 0 or np.random.rand() < np.exp(-delta_E / T):\n                  current_centers = candidate_centers\n                  current_energy = candidate_energy\n                  \n                  if current_energy < best_energy:\n                      best_energy = current_energy\n         \
    \             best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n                      best_radii = candidate_radii # Store the radii from the successful LP call\n                      stagnation_counter = 0\n\n          # Cooling\n          T *= alpha\n          stagnation_counter += 1\n          if stagnation_counter >= max_stagnation:\n              print(\"Stagnation detected, terminating.\")\n              break\n      \n      # Save the best artifact found\n      SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/sa_generator_artifact.npz'\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=best_centers, radii=best_radii)\n      \n      # Return a trivial packing as the script's purpose is artifact generation\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n```"
