tick: 143
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement my new research plan. I will start with a single, self-contained experiment. This script will generate a large number of candidate layouts using a physics-based approach, evaluate them all, and then save only the very best one. This is a \"champion selection\" strategy for finding a high-quality seed.\n\nThe physics simulation will be simple: it will treat the circle centers as particles that repel each other and are repelled by the walls of the unit square. By simulating their movement over time, they should settle into a low-energy, evenly distributed configuration. I will run this simulation multiple times from different random starts to generate a diverse pool of candidates.\n\nThe purpose of this script is purely artifact generation. It will then be followed by a separate refinement step.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generator Arc 3, Step 1: Physics-Based Seed Champion\"\ntags: \"physics simulation, seed\
    \ generation, generator, global optimization\"\nabstract: \"This experiment proposes a new method for generating a superior initial seed for the SOTA pipeline. It runs 100 independent, short physics simulations where circle centers are treated as repelling particles. It then evaluates all 100 resulting layouts using the fast exact_lp solver and saves only the single best configuration ('champion') to 'storage/cognito/physics_seed_artifact.npz'. This aims to find a higher quality starting point than the previous generators.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import os\n  import time\n\n  # --- Utility functions ---\n  def _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\n\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n      D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J],\
    \ axis=1)\n      m = len(I)\n      A_ub = np.zeros((m, n)); A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1; A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1; b_ub = D\n      c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(0, float(max(0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return (res.x, -res.fun) if res.success else (np.zeros(n), 0)\n\n  # --- Physics Simulation ---\n  def run_physics_sim(initial_centers, steps=200, dt=0.01, repulsion_strength=0.0005):\n      centers = np.copy(initial_centers)\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      velocity = np.zeros_like(centers)\n      \n      for _ in range(steps):\n          # Inter-particle repulsion\n          diff = centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :]\n          dist_sq = np.sum(diff**2, axis=-1)\n          dist_sq[np.arange(n), np.arange(n)] = np.inf # Avoid self-repulsion\n          inv_dist_sq = 1.0 / np.maximum(dist_sq, 1e-8)\n          force_vec = diff * inv_dist_sq[:, :, np.newaxis]\n          total_force = np.sum(force_vec,\
    \ axis=1) * repulsion_strength\n          \n          # Wall repulsion\n          total_force[:, 0] -= repulsion_strength / np.maximum(centers[:, 0]**2, 1e-6)\n          total_force[:, 0] += repulsion_strength / np.maximum((1 - centers[:, 0])**2, 1e-6)\n          total_force[:, 1] -= repulsion_strength / np.maximum(centers[:, 1]**2, 1e-6)\n          total_force[:, 1] += repulsion_strength / np.maximum((1 - centers[:, 1])**2, 1e-6)\n          \n          # Update velocity and position (Euler integration)\n          velocity += total_force * dt\n          velocity *= 0.95 # Damping\n          centers += velocity * dt\n          centers = np.clip(centers, 0.01, 0.99) # Keep particles inside\n          \n      return centers\n\n  # --- Main Artifact Generator ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      num_simulations = 100\n      best_score = -1\n      best_centers = None\n      best_radii = None\n      \n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=137)\n\n      print(f\"Running\
    \ {num_simulations} physics simulations to find the best seed...\")\n      for i in range(num_simulations):\n          # Generate a new random starting point for each simulation\n          initial_centers = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.9, size=(n, 2))\n          final_centers = run_physics_sim(initial_centers)\n          \n          # Evaluate the resulting layout with the LP solver\n          radii, score = exact_lp(final_centers)\n          \n          if score > best_score:\n              best_score = score\n              best_centers = final_centers\n              best_radii = radii\n              print(f\"New best seed found in sim {i}: Score = {score:.6f}\")\n\n      # Save the champion artifact\n      print(f\"\\nChampion seed found with score: {best_score:.6f}\")\n      SAVE_PATH = 'storage/cognito/physics_seed_artifact.npz'\n      os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(SAVE_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n      np.savez(SAVE_PATH, centers=best_centers, radii=best_radii)\n      \n      # Return a trivial\
    \ packing\n      return np.array([[0.1 + i*0.01, 0.1] for i in range(n)]), np.full(n, 0.001)\n```"
