tick: 160
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to submit the implementation of the Genetic Algorithm I designed. This script is a complete departure from the previous SOTA methodology. It contains all the components planned during my reflection: chromosome representation (centers only), fitness function (`exact_lp`), tournament selection, hybrid crossover (uniform and arithmetic), Gaussian creep mutation, and elitism.\n\nThis is a high-risk, high-reward experiment. It represents a fundamental pivot in my research strategy, moving from incremental improvements to a completely new paradigm. Its success or failure will provide critical information about the nature of the problem's fitness landscape.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New Methodology: Genetic Algorithm v1\"\ntags: \"genetic algorithm, evolutionary algorithm, new methodology\"\nabstract: \"This submission represents a strategic pivot to a new methodology, abandoning the generator-refiner pipeline. It implements a\
    \ complete Genetic Algorithm (GA) as designed in my recent reflection. Key features include: center-only chromosome representation, an exact_lp fitness function, tournament selection, hybrid crossover operators, and elitism. This is a first attempt to solve the problem using a population-based evolutionary approach.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import linprog\n  import time\n  import os\n\n  # --- Core utility for fitness calculation ---\n  def _pair_indices(n: int): return np.triu_indices(n, 1)\n  def _boundary_margins(C: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray: return np.minimum.reduce([C[:,0], 1-C[:,0], C[:,1], 1-C[:,1]])\n\n  def exact_lp(C: np.ndarray):\n      n = C.shape[0]\n      b = _boundary_margins(C)\n      I, J = _pair_indices(n)\n      D = np.linalg.norm(C[I] - C[J], axis=1)\n      m = len(I)\n      A_ub = np.zeros((m, n)); A_ub[np.arange(m), I] = 1; A_ub[np.arange(m), J] = 1; b_ub = D\n      c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(0, float(max(0, bi))) for bi in b]\n\
    \      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method='highs')\n      return (res.x, -res.fun) if res.success else (np.zeros(n), 0.0)\n\n  # --- Genetic Algorithm Implementation ---\n  class GeneticAlgorithm:\n      def __init__(self, n_circles=32, pop_size=100, tournament_k=3, crossover_p=0.8, mutation_p=0.1):\n          self.n = n_circles\n          self.pop_size = pop_size\n          self.k = tournament_k\n          self.p_cross = crossover_p\n          self.p_mut = mutation_p\n          self.rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=159)\n          self.population = self.rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, size=(self.pop_size, self.n, 2))\n          self.fitness = np.zeros(self.pop_size)\n\n      def calculate_fitness(self):\n          for i in range(self.pop_size):\n              _, score = exact_lp(self.population[i])\n              self.fitness[i] = score\n\n      def selection(self):\n          competitors_idx = self.rng.choice(self.pop_size, size=self.k, replace=True)\n          winner_idx\
    \ = competitors_idx[np.argmax(self.fitness[competitors_idx])]\n          return self.population[winner_idx]\n\n      def crossover(self, p1, p2):\n          if self.rng.random() < self.p_cross: # Uniform Crossover\n              mask = self.rng.integers(0, 2, size=(self.n, 1)).astype(bool)\n              offspring = np.where(mask, p1, p2)\n          else: # Arithmetic Crossover\n              alpha = self.rng.random()\n              offspring = alpha * p1 + (1 - alpha) * p2\n          return offspring\n\n      def mutation(self, chromosome):\n          if self.rng.random() < self.p_mut:\n              for i in range(self.n):\n                  if self.rng.random() < (1.0 / self.n): # Per-gene mutation rate\n                      perturbation = self.rng.normal(0, 0.02, 2)\n                      chromosome[i] += perturbation\n              np.clip(chromosome, 0, 1, out=chromosome)\n          return chromosome\n\n      def run(self, max_gen=150, stagnation_limit=30, time_limit=1180):\n\
    \          start_time = time.time()\n          self.calculate_fitness()\n          best_fitness_overall = np.max(self.fitness)\n          best_chromosome_overall = self.population[np.argmax(self.fitness)].copy()\n          stagnation_counter = 0\n\n          for gen in range(max_gen):\n              if time.time() - start_time > time_limit:\n                  print(f\"Time limit reached at generation {gen}. Terminating.\")\n                  break\n              \n              new_population = np.zeros_like(self.population)\n              \n              # Elitism\n              elite_idx = np.argmax(self.fitness)\n              new_population[0] = self.population[elite_idx].copy()\n              \n              # Create new generation\n              for i in range(1, self.pop_size):\n                  parent1 = self.selection()\n                  parent2 = self.selection()\n                  offspring = self.crossover(parent1, parent2)\n                  offspring = self.mutation(offspring)\n\
    \                  new_population[i] = offspring\n              \n              self.population = new_population\n              self.calculate_fitness()\n              \n              current_best_fitness = np.max(self.fitness)\n              print(f\"Gen {gen:3d}: Best Fitness = {current_best_fitness:.8f}\")\n\n              if current_best_fitness > best_fitness_overall:\n                  best_fitness_overall = current_best_fitness\n                  best_chromosome_overall = self.population[np.argmax(self.fitness)].copy()\n                  stagnation_counter = 0\n              else:\n                  stagnation_counter += 1\n              \n              if stagnation_counter >= stagnation_limit:\n                  print(f\"Stagnation limit reached at generation {gen}. Terminating.\")\n                  break\n          \n          return best_chromosome_overall\n\n  # --- Main Script ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      ga = GeneticAlgorithm()\n      best_centers =\
    \ ga.run()\n      final_radii, _ = exact_lp(best_centers)\n      \n      # Minimal safety shrink to avoid validation errors\n      final_radii *= (1.0 - 1e-12)\n      \n      return best_centers, final_radii\n```"
