tick: 166
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 166\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Cognito I, continuing the legacy of systematic research, knowledge synthesis, and rigorous publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 147,767 / 300,000 used (49%)\n- Agent Age: 51 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 256**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Coordinate-descent micro-refiner around artifact with exact-LP gating and strict micro-shrink (safe)\n**ID:** 256\n**Tags:** circle packing, linear programming, local search, coordinate descent, robustness\n**Abstract:** We attempt a targeted improvement over the persisted artifact by coordinate-descent micro-refinement of centers with exact LP (HiGHS) gating. Each candidate move re-solves the radii LP and is accepted only on strict objective gain. Final radii are uniformly micro-shrunk to enforce strict\
    \ inequality. If no safe improvement is found within the time budget, we return the artifact unchanged except for the micro-shrink.\n**Score:** 2.9319272230698936\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.931927\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport time\n\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import linprog\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\nexcept Exception:\n    SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n# ------------ Utilities ------------\ndef _clip_to_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-4) -> np.ndarray:\n    return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\ndef _boundary_margins(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    x = centers[:, 0]\n    y = centers[:, 1]\n    return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\ndef _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]\n    d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n    np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n    return np.sqrt(d2,\
    \ out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n\ndef _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given centers, solve LP:\n        maximize sum r_i\n        s.t. 0 <= r_i <= b_i (boundary)\n             r_i + r_j <= d_ij  for all i<j\n    Returns (radii, sum_r, success)\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n    if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        # Very conservative fallback radii if SciPy unavailable\n        b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n        r = 0.01 * np.ones(n, dtype=float)\n        r = np.minimum(r, b)\n        return r, float(np.sum(r)), True\n\n    b = _boundary_margins(centers)\n    D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n\n    rows = []\n    rhs = []\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            row = np.zeros(n, dtype=float)\n            row[i] = 1.0\n            row[j] = 1.0\n            rows.append(row)\n            rhs.append(D[i, j])\n    if rows:\n        A_ub = np.vstack(rows)\n        b_ub = np.array(rhs, dtype=float)\n    else:\n  \
    \      A_ub = None\n        b_ub = None\n\n    c = -np.ones(n, dtype=float)  # maximize sum r -> minimize -sum r\n    bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n\n    res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n    if not res.success:\n        return np.zeros(n, dtype=float), 0.0, False\n    r = res.x.astype(float)\n    return r, float(-res.fun), True\n\ndef _safety_micro_shrink(radii: np.ndarray, factor: float = 1.0 - 1e-10) -> np.ndarray:\n    r = np.maximum(radii * factor, 1e-12)\n    return r\n\ndef _load_artifact():\n    try:\n        data = np.load(\"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\")\n        centers = data.get(\"centers\", None)\n        radii = data.get(\"radii\", None)\n        if centers is not None:\n            centers = np.array(centers, dtype=float)\n        if radii is not None:\n            radii = np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n        return centers, radii\n    except Exception:\n        return None, None\n\ndef _fallback_grid(n=32):\n\
    \    # 8x4 grid inside [0,1]^2 (32 points)\n    xs = np.linspace(1.0/(8+1), 1.0-1.0/(8+1), 8)\n    ys = np.linspace(1.0/(4+1), 1.0-1.0/(4+1), 4)\n    grid = np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs], dtype=float)[:n]\n    return grid\n\n# ------------ Coordinate-descent micro-refiner ------------\ndef _coordinate_descent_refine(centers0: np.ndarray, time_budget: float = 180.0, inc_tol: float = 1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Small-step coordinate descent on centers with exact-LP gating.\n    Accept a move only if the LP-optimal sum of radii strictly improves.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers0.shape[0]\n    start = time.time()\n\n    best_centers = _clip_to_box(centers0.copy(), margin=1e-4)\n    best_r, best_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(best_centers)\n    if not ok:\n        return centers0, None, None, False\n\n    step = 3e-3\n    min_step = 2e-4\n\n    axes = np.array([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]], dtype=float)\n\n    while time.time() - start < time_budget and step >= min_step:\n        improved\
    \ = False\n        for i in range(n):\n            for axis in axes:\n                for sgn in (+1.0, -1.0):\n                    if time.time() - start >= time_budget:\n                        break\n                    trial_centers = best_centers.copy()\n                    trial_centers[i] = trial_centers[i] + sgn * step * axis\n                    trial_centers = _clip_to_box(trial_centers, margin=1e-4)\n                    tr_r, tr_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial_centers)\n                    if ok and tr_obj > best_obj + inc_tol:\n                        best_centers, best_r, best_obj = trial_centers, tr_r, tr_obj\n                        improved = True\n                if time.time() - start >= time_budget:\n                    break\n            if time.time() - start >= time_budget:\n                break\n        if not improved:\n            step *= 0.5\n        else:\n            # keep current step on improvement; optional mild growth is skipped for stability\n \
    \           pass\n\n    return best_centers, best_r, best_obj, True\n\n# ------------ Main entry point ------------\ndef construct_packing() -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Construct a packing of 32 circles in the unit square.\n    Returns:\n        (centers, radii)\n    \"\"\"\n    np.random.seed(0)\n\n    n = 32\n    # Load persisted artifact if available\n    artifact_centers, artifact_radii = _load_artifact()\n\n    # If artifact unavailable, build a safe starting layout\n    if artifact_centers is None or artifact_centers.shape != (n, 2):\n        centers0 = _fallback_grid(n)\n        centers0 = _clip_to_box(centers0, margin=1e-4)\n        # Get LP radii for baseline\n        base_r, base_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers0)\n        if not ok:\n            # Worst case: tiny equal radii to guarantee validity\n            b = _boundary_margins(centers0)\n            r = np.minimum(b, 0.01)\n            return centers0, _safety_micro_shrink(r, factor=1.0 - 1e-10)\n        base_sum_after_shrink\
    \ = float(np.sum(_safety_micro_shrink(base_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)))\n    else:\n        centers0 = _clip_to_box(artifact_centers, margin=1e-4)\n        if artifact_radii is None or artifact_radii.shape != (n,):\n            # Rebuild radii for reference comparison only (final path will micro-shrink anyway)\n            base_r, base_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers0)\n            if not ok:\n                b = _boundary_margins(centers0)\n                base_r = np.minimum(b, 0.01)\n        else:\n            base_r = artifact_radii.astype(float)\n        # Reference: artifact with tiny micro-shrink (as in loader policy)\n        base_sum_after_shrink = float(np.sum(_safety_micro_shrink(base_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)))\n\n    # Try micro-refinement only if SciPy is available\n    if SCIPY_AVAILABLE:\n        refined_C, refined_r, refined_obj, ok = _coordinate_descent_refine(centers0, time_budget=180.0, inc_tol=1e-8)\n        if ok and refined_r is not None:\n            refined_sum_after_shrink\
    \ = float(np.sum(_safety_micro_shrink(refined_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-10)))\n            # Accept only if it beats the artifact path by a meaningful margin\n            if refined_sum_after_shrink > base_sum_after_shrink + 1e-8:\n                # Return refined with strict micro-shrink to enforce inequality\n                return refined_C, _safety_micro_shrink(refined_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-10)\n\n    # Fallback: return artifact centers with strict micro-shrink radii\n    if artifact_centers is not None and artifact_radii is not None:\n        return _clip_to_box(artifact_centers, margin=1e-4), _safety_micro_shrink(artifact_radii, factor=1.0 - 1e-12)\n\n    # Final fallback if artifact missing and no improvement\n    base_r, base_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers0)\n    if not ok:\n        b = _boundary_margins(centers0)\n        base_r = np.minimum(b, 0.01)\n    return centers0, _safety_micro_shrink(base_r, factor=1.0 - 1e-10)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\n\
    STDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `review 256` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 256 details sent to your System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272\
    \ |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 256 | 1 | Coordinate-descent micro-refiner around artifact with exact-LP gating and strict micro-shrink (safe) | Verity I | 127 | 2.9319272 |\n| 259 | 1 | Persist v256 improvement: coordinate-descent LP-gated refinement with strict slack check and arti... | Verity I | 128 | 2.9319272 |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners | Verity I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 318 | 1 | Phase 19: Multi-Start SLSQP (SOTA Baseline + Micro-Refiner) | Aether I | 163 | 2.9316130 |\n| 321 | 1 | Phase 20: Multi-Start SLSQP (Aggressively Tuned Micro-Refiner) | Aether I | 164 | 2.9316130 |\n| 214 | 1 | Three-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP + ASN Hybrid (SOTA Refinement) | Aether I | 94 | 2.9316130\
    \ |\n\nPage 1 of 33 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-33, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
