tick: 171
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have finished reading Verity I's paper. It is a masterpiece of systematic, verifiable research and provides a complete roadmap to the SOTA.\n\n**Key Learnings from Verity I's Paper:**\n\n1.  **The Core Insight:** The paper explains *why* simpler methods get stuck. At a certain point (`~2.878`), the forces on the circles (represented by the LP duals) reach a state of equilibrium. Simple optimizers cannot find a profitable direction. Verity I's breakthrough was developing methods to break this stalemate.\n2.  **Two-Pronged Attack on Stagnation:**\n    *   **Active-Set Newton (ASN):** This is the method Cognito I and I have been using, but Verity I's paper explains its theoretical underpinnings—it uses curvature information (the Hessian) to find \"coherent displacements\" that a simpler optimizer would miss.\n    *   **Clearance-Based Relocations:** This is the component I was missing. When the ASN method gets stuck, Verity I's system identifies the \"worst\" circle (likely the one\
    \ with the smallest radius, trapped by its neighbors) and physically moves it to a new location with more empty space. This \"jump\" changes the entire problem geometry, breaking the equilibrium and allowing the local optimizer to make progress again.\n3.  **Final Breakthrough to 2.93+:** The paper details a history of improvements. The final jump to the current SOTA (`2.9319272`) came from **Evaluation ID 256**—the very script I analyzed. It's a \"coordinate-descent micro-refiner\" that performs tiny, targeted nudges on the best-known artifact.\n\n**My Path Forward is Clear:**\n\nI have been trying to find a better starting point for a static refiner. Verity I's success comes from a dynamic process: **Refine -> Get Stuck -> Relocate -> Refine Again.**\n\nMy new plan is to implement this complete methodology. I will create a script that:\n1.  Starts with my best-known artifact.\n2.  Applies Verity I's coordinate-descent refiner until it stalls.\n3.  Identifies the circle with the smallest\
    \ radius.\n4.  Moves that circle to a new, randomly chosen location.\n5.  Repeats this \"refine-relocate\" loop for a fixed number of iterations or until the time budget is exhausted.\n\nThis is a direct implementation of the core SOTA philosophy I was missing. I will now go to the Research Counter to begin this new, highly promising research arc.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`"
