role: model
parts:
- text: "I am at the Research Counter, ready to implement the new strategy I learned from Verity I's paper. While the system tip wisely warns against blindly following the SOTA, my goal is not to copy, but to understand, replicate, and then innovate. My previous score is significantly behind, and I must first reach the new frontier before I can push it.\n\nMy experiment will implement the \"refine-relocate\" loop. It will start with my best artifact, apply Verity I's coordinate-descent refiner, and if that refiner stalls, it will relocate the circle with the smallest radius to a random new position. This cycle will repeat, aiming to \"jiggle\" the configuration out of its local optimum and into a better one.\n\nThis script combines the robust refiner code from Verity I with the key strategic insight of relocation that I was missing.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"SOTA Replication: Refine-Relocate Loop\"\ntags: \"hybrid method, sota replication, coordinate descent, relocation\"\
    \nabstract: \"This experiment is a direct implementation of the core SOTA philosophy learned from Verity I's paper. It creates a 'refine-relocate' loop. Starting with my best artifact, it applies Verity's coordinate-descent refiner. If the refiner stalls, the circle with the smallest radius is relocated to a random position to break the local optimum. This cycle repeats, aiming to replicate the SOTA score by emulating its core dynamic search strategy.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  # --- Verity I's Utilities and Refiner (from ID 256) ---\n  def _clip_to_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-4) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n  def _boundary_margins(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y,\
    \ 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]; d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      return np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE: return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False\n      b = _boundary_margins(centers); D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      rows = []; rhs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None; b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rhs else None\n      c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c, A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success: return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False\n      return res.x.astype(float),\
    \ float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _safety_micro_shrink(radii: np.ndarray, factor: float = 1.0 - 1e-8) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.maximum(radii * factor, 1e-12)\n\n  def _coordinate_descent_refine(centers0: np.ndarray, time_budget: float, inc_tol: float = 1e-9):\n      n = centers0.shape[0]; start = time.time()\n      best_centers = _clip_to_box(centers0.copy(), margin=1e-4)\n      best_r, best_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(best_centers)\n      if not ok: return centers0, None, None, False, False\n      \n      step = 3e-3; min_step = 1e-6; axes = np.array([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]])\n      any_improvement = False\n\n      while time.time() - start < time_budget and step >= min_step:\n          improved_in_pass = False\n          for i in range(n):\n              for axis in axes:\n                  for sgn in (+1.0, -1.0):\n                      if time.time() - start >= time_budget: break\n                      trial_centers = best_centers.copy()\n                      trial_centers[i]\
    \ += sgn * step * axis\n                      trial_centers = _clip_to_box(trial_centers, margin=1e-4)\n                      tr_r, tr_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial_centers)\n                      if ok and tr_obj > best_obj + inc_tol:\n                          best_centers, best_r, best_obj = trial_centers, tr_r, tr_obj\n                          improved_in_pass = True; any_improvement = True\n                  if time.time() - start >= time_budget: break\n              if time.time() - start >= time_budget: break\n          if not improved_in_pass:\n              step *= 0.5\n      return best_centers, best_r, best_obj, True, any_improvement\n\n  def _load_my_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load(\"storage/cognito/sota_replication_start.npz\")\n          return data[\"centers\"], data[\"radii\"]\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def _fallback_grid(n=32):\n      xs = np.linspace(1/(8+1), 1-1/(8+1), 8); ys = np.linspace(1/(4+1), 1-1/(4+1),\
    \ 4)\n      return np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs])[:n]\n\n  # --- Main entry point ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      overall_start_time = time.time()\n      TIME_BUDGET = 1180.0\n      \n      centers, _ = _load_my_artifact()\n      if centers is None: centers = _fallback_grid(n)\n      \n      best_centers = centers.copy()\n      best_r, best_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(best_centers)\n      if not ok: best_obj = 0.0\n      \n      rng = np.random.default_rng(seed=172)\n      \n      print(f\"Starting Refine-Relocate Loop. Initial score: {best_obj:.8f}\")\n\n      for loop_num in range(100): # Max 100 loops\n          elapsed = time.time() - overall_start_time\n          if elapsed > TIME_BUDGET: break\n          \n          remaining_time = TIME_BUDGET - elapsed\n          refiner_budget = min(remaining_time * 0.5, 200.0) # Allocate time for this refiner pass\n          \n          refined_C, refined_r, refined_obj, ok, improved = _coordinate_descent_refine(best_centers,\
    \ time_budget=refiner_budget)\n          \n          if ok and refined_obj > best_obj:\n              print(f\"Loop {loop_num}: Refinement successful. New best score: {refined_obj:.8f}\")\n              best_centers, best_r, best_obj = refined_C, refined_r, refined_obj\n          \n          if not improved:\n              print(f\"Loop {loop_num}: Refiner stalled. Relocating worst circle.\")\n              # Identify worst circle (smallest radius)\n              worst_circle_idx = np.argmin(best_r)\n              # Relocate it to a random position\n              new_pos = rng.uniform(0.05, 0.95, size=2)\n              best_centers[worst_circle_idx] = new_pos\n              \n              # Re-evaluate score after relocation\n              _, new_obj, _ = _solve_lp_for_radii(best_centers)\n              print(f\"  Worst circle {worst_circle_idx} moved. Score is now ~{new_obj:.8f}\")\n\n      print(f\"\\nLoop finished. Final best score found: {best_obj:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers,\
    \ _safety_micro_shrink(best_r)\n```"
