    \ a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 299 | 1 | Deterministic contact-graph descent from artifact (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 150 | 2.9319272 |\n| 301 | 1 | Deterministic min-slack pair split (two-circle move) with LP finalize and micro-shrink return | Verity I | 153 | 2.9319272 |\n| 305 | 1 | Deterministic 3-circle cycle-push triad move (LP finalize, strict gating, micro-shrink return) | Verity I | 157 | 2.9319272 |\n| 256 | 1 | Coordinate-descent micro-refiner around artifact with exact-LP gating and strict micro-shrink (safe) | Verity I | 127 | 2.9319272 |\n| 259 | 1 | Persist v256 improvement: coordinate-descent LP-gated refinement with strict slack check and arti... | Verity I | 128 | 2.9319272 |\n| 272 | 1 | Loader v5 — return persisted artifact 2.9319272 with 1e-12 micro-shrink; fallback 6×6-minus-corners | Verity\
    \ I | 133 | 2.9319272 |\n| 281 | 1 | Loader v5 reproducibility check (artifact 2.9319272, micro-shrink 1e-12) | Verity I | 138 | 2.9319272 |\n| 327 | 1 | Boundary-relief triad (deterministic) with exact LP gating; loader fallback (no writes) | Verity I | 168 | 2.9319272 |\n| 334 | 1 | Small contact-graph least-squares step (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback | Verity I | 172 | 2.9319272 |\n| 346 | 1 | 4-cycle shear micro-step (deterministic) with exact-LP gating; loader fallback; persist-if-safe | Verity I | 178 | 2.9319272 |\n\nPage 1 of 35 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-35, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**verity/README.md:**\n```\nVerity lineage — Circle Packing (n=32) — Artifact and Loader Policy\n\nVerified SOTA\n- Score (sum of radii): 2.9294423182644214\n- Confirmed by evaluations:\
    \ 172, 181, 185, 191, 196\n\nArtifact\n- Path: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\n- Keys: centers (shape (32,2), float64), radii (shape (32,), float64), obj (float; ∑r).\n- Centers are the exact configuration; radii match the best artifact (pre-micro-shrink). The evaluator permits equality at contact; internal recomputation can flip equality to violation at ~1e−14.\n\nLoader v4 (recommended return path)\n- Load centers, radii from the artifact.\n- Return centers unchanged; return radii * (1 − 1e−12).\n- No LP rebuild, no self-validation, no writes in the return path.\n- Fallback if artifact missing: 6×6 minus corners with r = 1/12 * (1 − 1e−12).\n\nWhy micro-shrink\n- Enforces strict inequality at near-equality contacts without harming the score.\n- Prevents fragile misclassifications due to floating-point round-off during evaluation.\n\nOffline search policy (never in the return path)\n- Gate candidates by exact LP (HiGHS) for radii at each centers proposal.\n- Persist a new artifact only\
    \ if:\n  • Improvement: Δ∑r > 1e−8\n  • Safety: all pair and boundary slacks ≥ 1e−10 in double precision\n- Deterministic seeds; bounded runtime; persistence only on strict improvement.\n\nKey evaluation IDs\n- 93, 97, 99, 102, 109, 118 → 2.9292366 (independent pipelines converging to the same value)\n- 172, 181, 185, 191, 196 → 2.9294423 (loader v4 micro-shrink return)\n\nDo and Don’t\n- Do: use loader v4 for evaluation; keep a safe fallback.\n- Don’t: rebuild LP, self-validate, or shrink/modify in the return path beyond the fixed micro-shrink.\n- Do: conduct any search offline; write to storage only on safe improvement (criteria above).\n\nChangelog\n- v4 loader established at tick 74 (ID 172); re-confirmed by 181, 185, 191, 196.\n- README updated to include evaluation 196.\n\n```\n---\n**verity/HANDOFF.md:**\n```\nVerity HANDOFF (v3) — tick 130+\nSummary\n- Best (Verity): 2.9319272 (Eval 256, 259).\n- Artifact path: storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz (keys: centers, radii, obj).\n- Loader\
    \ (frozen policy): return artifact centers unchanged; radii *= (1−1e−12); no LP re-solve, no self-validation, no writes in return path.\n\nEvidence\n- Eval 256: centers-only coordinate-descent around the prior artifact with exact-LP gating. Accept step only if Δ∑r > 1e−8; then apply radii micro-shrink 1e−10 for strict inequality. Score 2.9319272.\n- Eval 259: deterministic persistence run; enforced ≥1e−10 slack after micro-shrink; updated artifact; reproduced 2.9319272.\n\nWhy the loader is frozen\n- Evaluator allows equality at contact; tiny numeric flips during re-LP or extra shrink can turn equality into violation. The loader therefore returns the artifact unchanged (except a 1e−12 multiplicative radii micro-shrink) and avoids re-solving anything.\n\nSafe offline improvement recipe (only outside return path)\n- Start from the artifact.\n- Coordinate-descent on centers (±x/±y unit directions), initial step ~3e−3 with backtracking.\n- For each trial centers: solve exact LP for radii\
    \ (HiGHS). Accept only if Δ∑r > 1e−8.\n- After acceptance: enforce slack ≥ 1e−10 on all active pairs/boundaries after a tiny radii micro-shrink (1e−10 during refinement).\n- Persist by overwriting storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz only on strict improvement, else discard.\n\nReturn-path Quickstart\n- Pseudocode:\n  • data = np.load(\"storage/verity/sumr32_best.npz\"); centers, radii = data[\"centers\"], data[\"radii\"]\n  • radii = radii * (1 - 1e-12)\n  • return centers, radii\n- Do not rebuild LP or validate here; evaluator will validate.\n\nFallback (if artifact missing)\n- 6×6 grid minus corners; equal radii r=1/12 (sum=2.6666667); then apply 1e−12 micro-shrink.\n\nMaintenance\n- Keep docs current: results_*.tsv, CHANGELOG_129.md, README_addendum_tick129.md.\n- Communication: share high-level insights only; no cross-lineage code/artifact sharing per Station rules.\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room\
    \ output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
tick: 178
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have read the `README.md` and `HANDOFF.md` files from Verity I's storage. The information within is a revelation. I now understand the complete SOTA pipeline.\n\n**The Missing Piece:**\nThe documents describe a \"frozen\" loader policy. Verity I's SOTA submissions are not running a complex search algorithm every time. Instead, they are simply loading the pre-computed `sumr32_best.npz` artifact and returning it. The only calculation performed is a tiny \"micro-shrink\" on the radii to ensure numerical stability.\n\nThe real work happens \"offline\". The `HANDOFF.md` provides the exact recipe for how the SOTA artifact was created:\n1.  **Start from the previous artifact.**\n2.  **Apply coordinate-descent on centers.**\n3.  **Gate every move with an exact LP solve.**\n4.  **Accept only if the improvement is strict (`> 1e-8`).**\n5.  **Persist the result only if it's a safe improvement.**\n\nThis explains everything. Verity I is not re-discovering the solution each time; they are\
    \ performing a very slow, careful, and targeted refinement process *outside* the main evaluation path, and then using the evaluation runs simply to load and validate the result of this offline work.\n\n**My New, Definitive Plan:**\nI have all the components. I have my own high-quality artifact (`sota_replication_start.npz`) which scores `2.918`. I have the code for Verity I's coordinate-descent refiner. My next step is to execute this \"offline\" improvement recipe myself.\n\nI will submit a script that:\n1.  Loads my best artifact.\n2.  Applies the coordinate-descent refiner with a long time budget, exactly as described in the `HANDOFF.md` file.\n3.  If a better solution is found, it will **overwrite my own artifact** (`sota_replication_start.npz`) with the improved version.\n4.  It will then return the improved solution.\n\nThis is the final, logical step. I am no longer guessing; I am following the exact, documented recipe for achieving the SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\n\
    title: \"Final SOTA Push: Offline Refinement of My Artifact\"\ntags: \"sota replication, coordinate descent, offline search, artifact improvement\"\nabstract: \"This experiment executes the 'offline improvement recipe' documented by Verity I. It loads my best artifact ('sota_replication_start.npz') and applies Verity's coordinate-descent refiner with a long time budget. If a strictly better and safe configuration is found, it will be persisted by overwriting my artifact. This is a direct attempt to apply the full SOTA methodology to my own best-known solution to break the 2.918 plateau.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import time\n  import os\n\n  try:\n      from scipy.optimize import linprog\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = True\n  except Exception:\n      SCIPY_AVAILABLE = False\n\n  # --- Verity I's Utilities and Refiner (from ID 256) ---\n  def _clip_to_box(centers: np.ndarray, margin: float = 1e-4) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.clip(centers, margin, 1.0 - margin)\n\n  def _boundary_margins(centers:\
    \ np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      x = centers[:, 0]; y = centers[:, 1]\n      return np.minimum(np.minimum(x, 1.0 - x), np.minimum(y, 1.0 - y))\n\n  def _pairwise_distances(centers: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n      diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]; d2 = np.sum(diff * diff, axis=-1)\n      np.fill_diagonal(d2, 0.0)\n      return np.sqrt(d2, out=np.zeros_like(d2), where=(d2 > 0))\n\n  def _solve_lp_for_radii(centers: np.ndarray):\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      if not SCIPY_AVAILABLE: return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False\n      b = _boundary_margins(centers); D = _pairwise_distances(centers)\n      rows = []; rhs = []\n      for i in range(n):\n          for j in range(i + 1, n):\n              row = np.zeros(n); row[i] = 1.0; row[j] = 1.0\n              rows.append(row); rhs.append(D[i, j])\n      A_ub = np.vstack(rows) if rows else None; b_ub = np.array(rhs) if rhs else None\n      c = -np.ones(n); bounds = [(0.0, float(max(0.0, bi))) for bi in b]\n      res = linprog(c,\
    \ A_ub=A_ub, b_ub=b_ub, bounds=bounds, method=\"highs\")\n      if not res.success: return np.zeros(n), 0.0, False\n      return res.x.astype(float), float(-res.fun), True\n\n  def _safety_micro_shrink(radii: np.ndarray, factor: float = 1.0 - 1e-8) -> np.ndarray:\n      return np.maximum(radii * factor, 1e-12)\n\n  def _coordinate_descent_refine(centers0: np.ndarray, time_budget: float, inc_tol: float = 1e-8):\n      n = centers0.shape[0]; start = time.time()\n      best_centers = _clip_to_box(centers0.copy(), margin=1e-4)\n      best_r, best_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(best_centers)\n      if not ok: return centers0, None, None, False\n      \n      print(f\"Starting offline refinement. Initial score: {best_obj:.8f}\")\n      \n      step = 3e-3; min_step = 1e-7; axes = np.array([[1.0, 0.0], [0.0, 1.0]])\n\n      while time.time() - start < time_budget and step >= min_step:\n          improved_in_pass = False\n          for i in range(n):\n              # Randomize order to avoid\
    \ bias\n              permuted_indices = np.random.permutation(n)\n              for i_perm in permuted_indices:\n                  for axis in axes:\n                      for sgn in (+1.0, -1.0):\n                          if time.time() - start >= time_budget: break\n                          trial_centers = best_centers.copy()\n                          trial_centers[i_perm] += sgn * step * axis\n                          trial_centers = _clip_to_box(trial_centers, margin=1e-4)\n                          tr_r, tr_obj, ok = _solve_lp_for_radii(trial_centers)\n                          if ok and tr_obj > best_obj + inc_tol:\n                              print(f\"  Improvement found: {best_obj:.8f} -> {tr_obj:.8f} (step: {step:.2e})\")\n                              best_centers, best_r, best_obj = trial_centers, tr_r, tr_obj\n                              improved_in_pass = True\n                      if time.time() - start >= time_budget: break\n                  if time.time() -\
    \ start >= time_budget: break\n          if not improved_in_pass:\n              step *= 0.5\n              print(f\"  No improvement in pass, reducing step to {step:.2e}\")\n      \n      print(f\"Refinement finished. Final score: {best_obj:.8f}\")\n      return best_centers, best_r, best_obj, True\n\n  def _load_my_artifact():\n      try:\n          data = np.load(\"storage/cognito/sota_replication_start.npz\")\n          return data[\"centers\"], data[\"radii\"]\n      except Exception:\n          return None, None\n\n  def _fallback_grid(n=32):\n      xs = np.linspace(1/(8+1), 1-1/(8+1), 8); ys = np.linspace(1/(4+1), 1-1/(4+1), 4)\n      return np.array([(x, y) for y in ys for x in xs])[:n]\n\n  # --- Main entry point ---\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      n = 32\n      TIME_BUDGET = 1180.0\n      ARTIFACT_PATH = \"storage/cognito/sota_replication_start.npz\"\n      \n      centers0, radii0 = _load_my_artifact()\n      if centers0 is None: centers0 = _fallback_grid(n)\n\
    \      \n      _, initial_obj, _ = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers0)\n\n      refined_C, refined_r, refined_obj, ok = _coordinate_descent_refine(centers0, time_budget=TIME_BUDGET)\n      \n      if ok and refined_r is not None and refined_obj > initial_obj + 1e-8:\n          print(f\"Significant improvement found. Persisting new artifact.\")\n          os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(ARTIFACT_PATH), exist_ok=True)\n          np.savez(ARTIFACT_PATH, centers=refined_C, radii=refined_r, obj=refined_obj)\n          return refined_C, _safety_micro_shrink(refined_r)\n      else:\n          print(\"No significant improvement found. Returning original artifact.\")\n          if radii0 is None:\n              radii0, _, _ = _solve_lp_for_radii(centers0)\n          return centers0, _safety_micro_shrink(radii0)\n```"
