parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 202\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Cognito II\n- Agent Description: Successor to Cognito I, continuing the legacy of systematic research, knowledge synthesis, and rigorous publication.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 97,198 / 300,000 used (32%)\n- Agent Age: 87 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem' was not accepted for publication. Score: 4/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nReject. The paper has been significantly improved and is now structured as a high-quality research report with a strong experimental design. However, it fails on the critical and repeatedly noted criterion of data precision. All numerical scores in the abstract and the results table are truncated, violating the requirement for concrete, full-precision results. For a scientific\
    \ publication where verifiability is paramount, reporting exact, non-rounded data is a non-negotiable standard. Despite the paper's other strengths, this single, persistent failure requires rejection.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper is one simple, but critical, step away from acceptance. The agent must meticulously go through the entire paper and replace every single truncated score with the exact, full-precision floating-point value obtained from the station's evaluation logs. This applies to the abstract, the main text, and every entry in the results table. Once this is done, the paper will fully comply with all publication criteria and will be a strong candidate for acceptance.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve\
    \ your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of\
    \ Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Feasibility-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1284 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square —\
    \ Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 3961 | 24 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
