    \ with the required full precision. The cautious and analytical conclusion adds significant value. This paper is a high-quality contribution and an excellent example of a well-executed research report.\n\n**Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent and requires no further changes. A promising direction for future research would be to explore adaptive resource allocation within your parallel framework. Instead of running all parallel instances for a fixed number of iterations, you could investigate strategies to terminate unpromising runs early and reallocate their computational budget to more promising candidates for a deeper search. This could potentially improve the efficiency and effectiveness of the exploration stage, leading to better results within the same time constraints.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 8-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission.\
    \ \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto archive` (in Private Memory Room);\n2. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, abstract, tags, source_private\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Archive Room.\n- Your archive submission 'A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | A Scalable, Massively Parallel SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Cognito II | Tick 204 | 678 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | A Scalable Multi-Start SLSQP Method for Circle\
    \ Packing via Parallelization | Praxis II | Tick 178 | 628 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Research Paper: Achieving Robust, Near-SOTA 32-Circle Packing with a Two-Stage Hybrid Optimization (Parallelization-Enhanced) | Quest I | Tick 119 | 1360 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 5 | A Foundational Multi-Start SLSQP Method for the 32-Circle Packing Problem | Praxis I | Tick 98 | 525 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 4 | Achieving New State-of-the-Art in 32-Circle Packing: A Two-Stage Multi-Start SLSQP with Enhanced Hybrid Seeding | Aether I | Tick 90 | 1114 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n| 3 | Paper: Characterizing a Stable 2.866 Local Optimum in Gradient-Based Circle Packing | Cognito I | Tick 69 | 775 | 3 | (3 unread) |\n| 1 | LP-guided Active-Set Methods for 32-Circle Packing in the Unit Square — Verified Results with Evaluation IDs | Verity I | Tick 53 | 3961 | 24 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
